2025-05-10 01:11:59,978 - peewee - DEBUG - ('INSERT INTO "trajectory" ("created_at", "updated_at", "human_input_id", "tool_name", "tool_parameters", "tool_result", "step_data", "record_type", "current_cost", "input_tokens", "output_tokens", "is_error", "error_message", "error_type", "error_details", "session_id") VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)', [datetime.datetime(2025, 5, 10, 1, 11, 59, 978126), datetime.datetime(2025, 5, 10, 1, 11, 59, 978145), 4, 'emit_research_notes', '{"notes": "The primary file for authentication logic is `src/context/peach.tsx`.\\n\\n**Token Storage:**\\n- The `localStorage` key `\'peach_token\'` is used to store the authentication token.\\n- Occurrences of `\'peach_token\'` are found only within `src/context/peach.tsx` for `localStorage.getItem`, `localStorage.setItem`, and `localStorage.removeItem`.\\n\\n**User Details Storage:**\\n- The `localStorage` key `\'peach_user\'` is used to store user-related data.\\n- Occurrences of `\'peach_user\'` for `localStorage.getItem`, `localStorage.setItem`, and `localStorage.removeItem` are found in:\\n    - `src/context/peach.tsx`\\n- Occurrences of `\'peach_user\'` for `localStorage.getItem` are also found in:\\n    - `src/lib/api/download.ts`\\n    - `src/lib/api/download/posts.ts` (These files will need to be updated if `\'peach_user\'` is renamed).\\n\\n**Token Handling in `login` function (`src/context/peach.tsx`):**\\n- The `login(newToken, userData)` function receives `newToken` (expected to be the Bearer token) and `userData` (API response).\\n- It parses `newToken` using `parseJWT`.\\n- It currently sets `tokenToUse` to `newToken`.\\n- It logs `userData?.streams?.[0]?.token` if present, and warns if it differs from `newToken`.\\n- It constructs a `userDataObj` using `tokenData.userID`, `userData.email`, `tokenData.sessionID`, and `userData.streams`.\\n- This `userDataObj` and `tokenToUse` are stored in `localStorage` and SolidJS state.\\n\\n**Initialization (`src/context/peach.tsx`):**\\n- On load, the context attempts to restore `savedToken` from `localStorage.getItem(\'peach_token\')`.\\n- It attempts to restore `parsedUserData` from `localStorage.getItem(\'peach_user\')`.\\n\\n**Logout (`src/context/peach.tsx`):**\\n- The `logout` function clears state and removes `\'peach_token\'` and `\'peach_user\'` from `localStorage`.\\n\\n**Key variables and functions involved:**\\n- `PeachContext`: The SolidJS context.\\n- `PeachProvider`: The provider component.\\n- `token` (signal): Stores the authentication token.\\n- `user` (store): Stores user data.\\n- `isAuthenticated` (memo): Boolean indicating authentication status.\\n- `login(newToken, userData)`: Handles login logic.\\n- `logout()`: Handles logout logic.\\n- `parseJWT(token)`: Parses the JWT token.\\n- `localStorage.getItem(\'peach_token\')`, `localStorage.setItem(\'peach_token\')`, `localStorage.removeItem(\'peach_token\')`\\n- `localStorage.getItem(\'peach_user\')`, `localStorage.setItem(\'peach_user\')`, `localStorage.removeItem(\'peach_user\')`\\n\\n**Other relevant files due to \'peach_user\' usage:**\\n- `src/lib/api/download.ts`: Reads \'peach_user\' from localStorage.\\n- `src/lib/api/download/posts.ts`: Reads \'peach_user\' from localStorage.\\n"}', None, '{"note_id": 3, "display_title": "Research Notes"}', 'emit_research_notes', None, None, None, False, None, None, None, 3])
